# Component Development Guidelines

## TypeScript Requirements
- Use TypeScript interfaces for all props
- Enable strict mode for type safety
- Add proper return types for functions
- Implement proper prop validation

## Component Structure
```typescript
interface ComponentProps {
  // Define all props with proper types
}

export default function Component({ prop1, prop2 }: ComponentProps) {
  // Component logic
  return (
    // JSX with proper TypeScript
  );
}
```

## React Best Practices
- Use functional components with hooks
- Implement React.memo for expensive components
- Use proper dependency arrays in useEffect
- Lift state up to parent components when needed

## State Management Flow
- Use React useState for component state
- Lift state up to ImageEditor component for shared state
- Follow the flow: upload → prompt → generate → display

## Loading States & Error Handling
- Implement proper loading states for all async operations
- Add error boundaries and validation
- Provide user-friendly error messages
- Implement retry mechanisms where appropriate

## Performance
- Use React.memo for expensive components
- Lazy load components when appropriate
- Optimize image handling (compression, format conversion)